    "explanation": "To the rider and to the driver.\n\nThis was a metered RYDE_X trip (TRP-02822) from Blk 640 Jurong West St 61 to Blk 456 Hougang Ave 10 on 13 September 2026, charged at SGD 9.28.\n\nROUTE DEVIATION — ESTABLISHED, AND ON THE TRACE. POL-RD-01 makes gps_trace.trace_distance_km govern, and it is 4.05 km; trip_record.actual_distance_km (4.00 km) is a rounded convenience copy that may not be cited for the threshold test. Against the booked optimal of 3.20 km the excess is 0.85 km, or 26.56% of optimal. Both establishment tests pass: 0.85 km is greater than 0.80 km absolute and greater than 20% of optimal (0.64 km). On the rounded 4.00 km copy the excess would be exactly 0.80 km and would have failed the strict 'greater than' test, so which artifact governs decides this case and the trace governs. The trace is NOT impaired for policy purposes: 37 fixes at a 10-second sample interval, 100% coverage, no gaps and a maximum inter-fix gap of 0.0 s, so none of POL-RD-07(a) to (c) is met, no independent corroboration under POL-RD-07(ii) was required, and no POL-RD-10(3) escalation arises.\n\nTHE REFUND IS ARITHMETIC. fare_model is METERED and quoted_fare_sgd is null, so POL-RD-11 does not close the distance route and POL-RD-02 runs. On separate lines: charged_total 9.28; recomputed_fare = ((3.80 base fare + 0.75 x 3.20 optimal km [2.40] + 0.28 x 6.0 optimal min [1.68]) x the surge multiplier 1.0 read from the fare breakdown) + 0.80 platform fee + 0.00 ERP/tolls + 0.00 waiting fee - 0.00 promo discount = 8.68; refund = 9.28 - 8.68 = 0.60. That is above the SGD 0.50 de minimis floor, so NO_ACTION does not apply, and at 6.47% of charged_total it is far below the 90% that would make it a full refund. The rider's claim to the whole SGD 9.28 is not supported; the arithmetic yields 0.60, not 9.28, and the outcome is PARTIAL_REFUND of SGD 0.60.\n\nNO EXCUSING CLAUSE APPLIES. No endpoint was amended after booking (POL-RD-05: pickup_amended_at, dropoff_amended_at and amended_optimal_distance_km are all null), so the booked optimal of 3.20 km stands. No rider-requested detour can be shown: the chat log carries zero messages, so there is no instruction and no waypoint_hint (POL-RD-04). The trip was not pooled (POL-RD-12: vehicle_type RYDE_X, solo_optimal_distance_km null). No traffic cause exonerates the excess: there is no advisory on file (POL-RD-03 is unavailable, POL-RD-13), and the driver's statement 'Followed the app' names neither an artifact nor a clause, so it carries no weight under POL-RD-08. The missing advisory artifact EV-ADVIS-02822-01 is MISSING at weight 0.0, but no party cited it as the ground of an exculpatory excuse, so it is a gap in the bundle, not a POL-RD-10(5) trigger.\n\nBILLING LINES AND COMPENSATION. The fare carries no ERP, no tolls, no airport surcharge and no waiting fee (all 0.00), so POL-RD-09 corrects nothing and no POL-RD-09(4) billing-integrity finding or referral arises; POL-RD-09(1) simply confirms nothing is added on top of the 0.60. No driver compensation is due: the billed distance (4.0 km) falls only 0.05 km short of the trace distance, far below the 1.0 km shortfall POL-RD-04 requires.\n\nPROFILE EVIDENCE. No repeat-deviation pattern is established: driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 1 (below 3) and 1 against driver_profile.completed_trips_90d of 402 is 0.0025 (below 0.05), so the POL-RD-06 uplift and the POL-RD-06(c) conduct referral do not arise; in any event the excess of 0.85 km is below both materiality gates. rider_profile.deviation_claims_60d is 0, so no extra corroboration was required. Every other field on either profile — including the lifetime counter prior_deviation_flags — is context only under POL-GEN-01 and was not used as a ground.\n\nDISCARDED CLAIM. The rider's submission that no traffic clause excuses the excess cited the impaired advisory EV-ADVIS-02822-01 without disclosing its impairment (MISSING_ARTIFACT, weight 0.0). It was discarded on that ground by the mechanical check, and the conclusion it drew — that no advisory is on file — is reached here from the absent artifact itself, not from that claim.\n\nNO REFERRAL FIRES: no POL-RD-06(c) conduct review, no POL-RD-09(4) billing-integrity referral and no POL-NS-05(ii) false-arrival record. The monetary effect, SGD 0.60, is below the SGD 8.00 execution threshold, so it executes automatically. This ruling is provisional and either party may appeal it once within 30 days under POL-GEN-04."
